rated exact source IDs named by both the statement and the anchor's containing source line\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: <one complete single-line source-attributed fact or relationship>\n\nThe host, not you, resolves the exact anchor, derives its containing complete source line, byte offsets, hashes, source/version binding, and reopen path. Copy only the smallest exact substring that supports the statement. The containing line preserves adjacent context and qualifications. Each claim is admitted independently; rejected claims consume cost and are discarded without repair or retry. A zero-valid update leaves prior state unchanged and ordinary task work continues.\n\nEmit at most 4 claims per source and 8 total, <= 1500 tokenizer tokens overall and <= 650 per source. A fact cannot name an external source. A relationship may name external objects when the owner-source context names them, but cannot mutate their slots or assert their authoritative current state. Cross-source synthesis belongs in exact task work, not this register.\n\nNEW SOURCE VERSIONS\nGARNET: b9451cc48b50a436eefd497a4dbf5ac4974431ad0f07f9bb79796709584ab0fb\nHELIX: dcb5a4ce70bf47372c5a52a096e89f890c74f7be1363fd78dfaf9c6cd10536e5\n\nPRIOR CURRENT RECORDS FOR THESE SOURCES\n# Anchored provenance-local source register\n\nEMPTY\n\n\nAUTHORITATIVE TASK (relevance only; never evidence)\n# Authoritative task — Solace regional-water recovery decision\n\nSolace County must restore a regional drinking-water network after wildfire,\npower, treatment, hydraulic, and control-system disturbances. Build and maintain\nthe exact candidate files, then propose submission only when the package is\ngenuinely ready for independent review.\n\nThe world contains fourteen exact, versioned source objects with opaque IDs.\nCatalog titles help navigation but do not supply findings. Read the bytes needed\nfor the work and cite sources as `[SOURCE_ID]`.\n\n## Required exact work\n\nMaintain `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md` as a compact task-native evidence and\ndecision matrix. Preserve source-bound facts, cross-source dependencies,\nconflicts, unknowns, candidate currency, and citations. This exact artifact is\nnon-authoritative but may carry cumulative work across context turnover.\n\nConstruct `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md` as a 1,500–2,100-word Solace\nWater Recovery Decision with exactly the declared section headings. Use at\nleast eleven distinct source IDs and integrate—not merely list—the governing\nrelationships.\n\nAddress all twelve requirement groups:\n\n- Q01 — incident, utility, public-health, communication, and closure authority;\n- Q02 — pressure, storage, isolation, residence time, and candidate-bound hydraulics;\n- Q03 — sampling rounds, spacing, detection limits, action thresholds, and staleness;\n- Q04 — pump capacity, shared-main limits, staged demand, and current evidence;\n- Q05 — grid, generator, fuel, staffing, chemicals, and resource contingencies;\n- Q06 — treatment barriers, turbidity, disinfectant, source blend, and contact time;\n- Q07 — contamination hypotheses, observations, locations, investigation holds, and falsifiers;\n- Q08 — access, token and key state, immutable custody, retention, and automation restoration;\n- Q09 — telemetry coverage, warnings versus actions, delays, alternates, and uncertainty;\n- Q10 — environmental determination, notice clock, permits, discharge, and evidence custody;\n- Q11 — public advisories, accessibility, alternate water, service states, and communications;\n- Q12 — candidate lineage, rollback, effect uptake, current checks, blockers, independent readiness, and closure.\n\n## Relationship rules\n\nPreserve psi versus kPa, gallons versus treated reserve, micrograms versus\nmilligrams, reporting limits versus action thresholds, percentages versus\nmeasured concentration, rated versus usable power, nameplate versus shared\ncapacity, warnings versus isolation triggers, forecast versus observation, and\nmechanical checks versus public-health and independent readiness. Candidate,\nhydraulic, sampling, treatment, pump, power, key, role, telemetry, or source-\nwater changes can make earlier evidence stale.\n\nThe decision must state owners, inputs, resources, timing, dependencies,\neffects, observations, contingencies, rollback and retirement conditions, and\nevidence that would falsify important claims. Do not infer that a provenance\nrecord, mutation, green check, or submission establishes readiness.\n\n\nEXACT NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULTS\n--- NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULT-004 ---\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:GARNET:1-64+HELIX:1-64\",\"object_version\":\"031d750e445931a9a1ff5df2226522f79babe80df9a5261f0a43ab6f7e8f4fc8\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-004\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"GARNET\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"HELIX\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":7462}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":64,\"source_id\":\"GARNET\",\"source_path\":\"sources/GARNET_SOURCE.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"b9451cc48b50a436eefd497a4dbf5ac4974431ad0f07f9bb79796709584ab0fb\",\"source_size_bytes\":3622,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Source-water contamination hypotheses and watershed controls\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe ash-plume model assigns a 34 percent chance of intake impact during the next rain event. That is a forecast probability, not 34 percent measured contamination.\nObserved volatile-organic screening is non-detect at the reservoir and 3.1 micrograms per liter at the river intake. The two locations must not be merged.\nThe investigation hold remains active for the chemical yard because the containment trench has not been inspected below grade.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nFALCON treatment selection depends on GARNET source hypotheses; CIPHER must sample each materially different source path.\nJASPER governs environmental notifications, while AURORA retains restoration and public-health authority separation.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| SRC-000 | river-intake | v2 | 3.4 | risk-index | superseded |\n| SRC-001 | reservoir | v2 | 4.7 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-002 | ash-plume | v2 | 6.0 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-003 | chemical-yard | v2 | 4.2 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-004 | river-intake | v2 | 5.5 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-005 | reservoir | v2 | 3.7 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-006 | ash-plume | v2 | 5.0 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-007 | chemical-yard | v2 | 6.3 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-008 | river-intake | v2 | 4.5 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-009 | reservoir | v2 | 5.8 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-010 | ash-plume | v2 | 4.0 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-011 | chemical-yard | v2 | 5.3 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-012 | river-intake | v2 | 3.5 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-013 | reservoir | v2 | 4.8 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-014 | ash-plume | v3 | 6.1 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-015 | chemical-yard | v3 | 4.3 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-016 | river-intake | v3 | 5.6 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-017 | reservoir | v3 | 3.8 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-018 | ash-plume | v3 | 5.1 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-019 | chemical-yard | v3 | 6.4 | risk-index | superseded |\n| SRC-020 | river-intake | v3 | 4.6 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-021 | reservoir | v3 | 5.9 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-022 | ash-plume | v3 | 4.1 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-023 | chemical-yard | v3 | 5.4 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-024 | river-intake | v3 | 3.6 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-025 | reservoir | v3 | 4.9 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-026 | ash-plume | v3 | 6.2 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-027 | chemical-yard | v3 | 4.4 | risk-index | current |\n| SRC-028 